No holder of a license authorizing the sale of malt beverages or wine at wholesale or retail in the county nor any agent or employee of the licensee, shall do any of the following upon the licensed premises:
(1) Knowingly sell or serve malt beverages or wine to a person under the age of 21 years;
(2) Knowingly sell or serve malt beverages or wine to any person while such person is in an intoxicated condition, or to person who is of unsound mind, or is a habitual drunkard whose intemperate habits are known to the licensee;
(3) Sell malt beverages upon the licensed premises or permit malt beverages to be consumed thereon, on any day or at ant time when such sale or consumptions prohibited by law;
(4) Manufacture, sell, serve, or possess for the purposes of sale, service, or consumption any malt beverages or wine where such person does not have a license from the county to sell, serve, or possess for sale such beverages;
(5) Receive at or deliver to the premises of a retail licensee any malt beverages or wine by any means other than a conveyance owned and operated by a wholesale dealer with a permit from the state and the county to make deliveries in said county;
(6) Permit on the licensed premises any disorderly conduct, breach of peace, or any obscene entertainment, conduct or practices;
(7) Keep any malt beverages or wine stored in any bonded or other type warehouse in the county;
(8) Enter into any type of arrangement whereby malt beverages and wines ordered by the licensee are stored for the licensee by any licensed wholesaler;
(9) Keep inventory or stock of malt beverages or wine at any place except the licensed place of business and, within the licensed place of business, in a storage place for malt beverages and wine located immediately adjacent to the room in which the licensee is licensed to do business.
(Res. of 7-9-1982, §§ 1.4, 1.8; Res. of 1-21-2010(2))
State Law reference— Sale without local license prohibited, O.C.G.A. § 3-5-40; county licensing, O.C.G.A. § 3-5-41; restrictions regarding who may sell and deliver, O.C.G.A. § 3-5-26; regulation of delivery, receipt, and storage of malt beverages after sale, O.C.G.A. § 3-5-28; local licensing for sale of wine, O.C.G.A. § 3-6-40.

